      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:03:01Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(verify): a lateral rapid is re-read against the stock's top under it\n\nThe rapid-in-stock law caps every column at the stock's highest point.\n#1091 (PR #1098) re-reads a convicted vertical dive against the stock\nand part solids under the tool stack; lateral rapids kept the flat cap,\nso a drill's link at its retract plane across the low part of a stepped\n\"from model\" stock was convicted as if the boss stood under it, and the\npost was blocked.\n\nacquit_by_stock_top now re-reads an upright lateral rapid the same way:\neach band of the stack over the capsule it sweeps along the move,\nagainst the highest stock or part facet within its radius, the tip at\nthe rapid's lowest end. It only removes convictions and fails closed as\nthe dive does. A dive is the zero-length capsule (dist2_seg_tri of a\npoint is dist2_tri), so its verdicts are unchanged.\n\nPinned by stepped_stock_link (a part-sourced drill's link over the low\nstep passes and posts; across the boss, or with the boss under the rim\nalong the way, it is convicted and blocks the post) and the stock_top\nunit tests (traverse acquitted, crossing the boss, boss under the rim,\nholder band, part, fail-closed). #1098's\nonly_upright_column_dives_are_re_read now expects its diagonal dive\nacquitted, and posed still convicted.\n\nStacked on #1098.\n\nFixes #1095\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
